  "core_idea": "**Yourself** refers back to the person spoken to, either as the object of that person's own action or to show that they, no one else, did or were affected by something.",
  "senses": [
    {
      "n": 1,
      "signpost": "reflexive",
      "definition": "used as the object of a verb or preposition when the action affects the person spoken to, the same person who is the subject",
      "explanation": "**Yourself** is used when the subject and the object of the same clause refer to the same person: *did you hurt yourself?* It is not just another way of saying **you**: use **you** when the object is a different person from the subject, *I'll call you*, not *I'll call yourself*.",
